The business requirements should output in `Enhancements/[x]/BusinessRequirements.md` under the repository root, with concrete content below each corresponding point:
	•	Business goals (increase X, reduce Y)
	•	Product scope
	•	High-level constraints (legal, budget, time)
	•	Success metrics (KPIs)

The functional requirements should output in `Enhancements/[x]/FunctionalRequirements.md` under the repository root, with concrete content below each corresponding point:
	•	Use cases / user stories
	•	Functional specs
	•	State transitions
	•	Business rules

The non-functional requirements should output in `Enhancements/[x]/Non-FunctionalRequirements.md` under the repository root, with concrete content below each corresponding point:
	•	Performance SLAs
	•	Availability targets
	•	Security requirements
	•	Scalability limits
	•	Compliance rules

The logical design should output in `Enhancements/[x]/LogicalDesign.md` under the repository root, with concrete content below each corresponding point:
	•	System structure (components, modules, domains)
	•	Responsibilities and interfaces
	•	Data & behavior models
	•	Control & interaction flows
	•	Invariants & constraints


The technical design should output in `Enhancements/[x]/TechnicalDesign.md` under the repository root, with concrete content below each corresponding point:
	•	Concrete technologies
	•	Deployment topology
	•	Data storage choices
	•	Protocols and formats
	•	Resource sizing
	•	Failure & recovery mechanisms

The implementation should output in `Enhancements/[x]/Implementation.md` under the repository root, with concrete content below each corresponding point:
	•	Plan
	•	Running code artifacts (binaries, services, packages)
	•	Source code aligned with design
	•	Automated tests
	•	Buildable & deployable units
